# A terminal UI for the firewall the profile already configures.
#
# ufw is in the core because a server has to be firewalled; reading and editing
# its rules from a TUI is not something a machine needs to boot, so it is here.
# tui-firewall previews the exact command line of every change before running
# it and keeps no state of its own, so it adds no daemon and no listening
# socket. It was called `fwall` until the tools moved to the tui-tools
# organization; the package replaces that name.
tui-firewall
